1
00:00:26,484 --> 00:00:27,861
No!

2
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:56,890
As a pair, we're unstoppable.
I can take down my father.

3
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:59,768
I can't watch that man win.
I won't let it happen.

4
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:02,103
He's not my real father.

5
00:01:03,646 --> 00:01:05,482
Or how you made a girl go blind.
Everything.

6
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:07,609
You can't even properly operate
on your own.

7
00:01:10,945 --> 00:01:11,946
It's okay.

8
00:01:14,741 --> 00:01:16,743
What exactly are you so afraid of?

9
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:20,830
I can't believe you're still acting like
plastic surgery is taboo.

10
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:22,665
It can't be me. It has to be you!

11
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:24,959
Do you have a better plan?

12
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:28,463
If she says she wants to die,
you'll kill her? Have you lost your mind?

13
00:01:28,546 --> 00:01:30,799
She's asking for one last chance
to be beautiful.

14
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:33,551
I'm a doctor.
I won't operate on someone who isn't sick.

15
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:35,386
Shit! I won't forgive you.

16
00:01:36,096 --> 00:01:37,889
- Sorry?
- I'll say it again.

17
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:39,224
I will never forgive you.

18
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:43,937
He was the absolute worst.

19
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:46,648
What was Dad like?

20
00:01:58,618 --> 00:02:01,329
DECONSTRUCTION

21
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:03,957
Fumi Numata, 33.
Passenger on a motorcycle accident.

22
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:06,251
- She needs to get to the OR.
- Don't worry.

23
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:08,461
Fumi? Fumi, talk to me. Are you okay?

24
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:10,213
We're gonna take care of you.

25
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:12,507
Just gonna move you. One, two, three.

26
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:13,424
She's on.

27
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:15,093
- We've got you.
- Where's Fumi?

28
00:02:15,176 --> 00:02:17,971
- Checking for breaks.
- Miss, you're in good hands.

29
00:02:18,054 --> 00:02:20,223
She needs a transfusion.
Let's get an IV in her.

30
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:21,683
- Setting up.
- Fumi!

31
00:02:21,766 --> 00:02:24,727
I'm gonna be honest with you.
She sustained severe injuries.

32
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:28,148
Multiple fractures all over her body.

33
00:02:28,231 --> 00:02:29,607
But she'll heal, right?

34
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,568
<i>It's not like she's gonna die.</i>

35
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:33,778
<i>No, not likely.</i>

36
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:36,614
<i>Seeing as there's no visible trauma</i>
<i>to her brain or spinal cord,</i>

37
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:38,616
with some time and treatments,

38
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:41,077
she'll make a full recovery
and get back to normal life.

39
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:45,206
With that said, things for her
won't be exactly the same as they were.

40
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:49,502
She suffered a strong impact to her face
when she hit the ground.

41
00:02:49,586 --> 00:02:50,628
I need gauze.

42
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,630
There's also significant tissue loss.

43
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:53,548
Tissue loss?

44
00:02:53,631 --> 00:02:56,718
The actual term is "facial disfigurement."

45
00:02:56,801 --> 00:02:59,262
She will have permanent scarring

46
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:01,014
and changes to her appearance.

47
00:03:01,097 --> 00:03:02,640
I need a new monitor as well.

48
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:03,725
<i>Whatever the case,</i>

49
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:06,102
<i>she'll need to be hospitalized</i>
<i>as she recovers.</i>

50
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:09,105
<i>It would be best to inform her work</i>
<i>that she'll need medical leave.</i>

51
00:03:09,189 --> 00:03:10,356
<i>I understand.</i>

52
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:12,502
Accident?

53
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:16,547
It'll take her several months
to recover, I'm sure.

54
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,312
Congratulations, Governor.

55
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:33,106
You made it happen.

56
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:34,774
All thanks to you, Dr. Rin.

57
00:04:38,361 --> 00:04:39,237
Please sit.

58
00:04:40,989 --> 00:04:43,449
Where's, uh, that lady friend of yours?

59
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:45,618
She had an emergency to take care of.

60
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:48,830
I'm sorry. I'm afraid
it's just you and me today, Governor.

61
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:50,665
That sounds perfect.

62
00:04:52,625 --> 00:04:54,294
It's all my fault.

63
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,879
I'm truly sorry

64
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:00,341
from… the bottom…

65
00:05:01,634 --> 00:05:03,469
Honestly, I don't even know what to say.

66
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:05,138
Don't worry, okay?

67
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:07,098
Macky, you were injured as well, got it?

68
00:05:07,181 --> 00:05:08,558
But Fumi…

69
00:05:09,892 --> 00:05:13,062
She was saying how she felt better finally
after talking to Takeru.

70
00:05:13,146 --> 00:05:16,190
I'm really sorry.
I'm really, really sorry.

71
00:05:16,274 --> 00:05:19,610
A prominent member of
the current governing party approached me.

72
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:24,574
And they invited me to have dinner
with Chairman Arata Tohyama.

73
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:26,701
So then,

74
00:05:28,119 --> 00:05:30,079
what do you intend to do, Governor?

75
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,917
Well, I placed all my chips
on you, Dr. Rin,

76
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:37,003
and that turned out pretty good.

77
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:39,922
For this project,
I'm gonna need to go all out.

78
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:42,633
I want someone who represents the future.

79
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:46,137
Something so massive
needs a face people can trust.

80
00:05:49,974 --> 00:05:52,643
I think my drinks will taste
extra good tonight.

81
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:57,190
I've been thinking of the chairman

82
00:05:57,273 --> 00:05:59,108
and always wondered…

83
00:05:59,942 --> 00:06:02,195
Why retire so early

84
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:06,783
if his intention was
to go up against you in the first place?

85
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:08,951
As far back as I can remember,

86
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:11,704
I don't believe there was ever
an official reason.

87
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:15,541
So as a special favor
in celebration of my reelection,

88
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:16,459
would you tell me?

89
00:06:18,503 --> 00:06:21,255
All right, then,
but only as a special favor.

90
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:25,093
The full story is that

91
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:29,305
the chairman had chronic kidney disease
most of his life.

92
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:32,809
And he searched a long time for a donor.

93
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:33,810
<i>Accident?</i>

94
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:35,686
That's unfortunate.

95
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:40,983
<i>But despite his patience,</i>
<i>his opportunity never came.</i>

96
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:42,902
His condition got so bad

97
00:06:42,985 --> 00:06:44,779
that he was on the verge
of kidney failure.

98
00:06:44,862 --> 00:06:46,155
Then could that be

99
00:06:46,989 --> 00:06:48,616
the reason that he went abroad was…

100
00:06:48,699 --> 00:06:50,868
He ran out of time and patience,

101
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:53,955
and decided to use his connections
for a transplant abroad.

102
00:06:54,038 --> 00:06:55,540
- Why don't you rest?
- Good idea.

103
00:06:55,623 --> 00:06:58,960
<i>You still love the chairman,</i>
<i>Dr. Rin, don't you?</i>

104
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:02,672
Why the curiosity?

105
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:07,260
A transplant abroad could be in violation
of organ transplant laws.

106
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:09,929
It would have been easy for you
to expose the secret

107
00:07:10,012 --> 00:07:11,639
during the conflict with the family,

108
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:13,808
<i>but you chose not to.</i>

109
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:19,689
I needed to keep my trump card
for the right moment.

110
00:07:19,772 --> 00:07:20,690
No, no.

111
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:25,194
It was love. I know it.

112
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:29,073
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

113
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:50,553
Numata.

114
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:52,847
It's getting late.

115
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:55,558
Why don't we reschedule the meeting
for another day?

116
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:58,060
Are you coming over to my house?

117
00:07:58,144 --> 00:07:59,395
Oh, it's Mommy.

118
00:08:00,229 --> 00:08:02,356
Hey! Give me back my ball!

119
00:08:03,232 --> 00:08:04,150
<i>Ms. Numata.</i>

120
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:05,193
Hmm.

121
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:09,238
That project right there, the diorama.

122
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:12,241
- Fumi made it during class.
- Hmm?

123
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:14,827
Seriously?

124
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:16,496
Honey?

125
00:08:17,288 --> 00:08:19,457
It's beautiful.

126
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:26,464
Apparently, according to our art teacher,
she seems to have a natural talent.

127
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:29,175
Fumi may be what we call "gifted."

128
00:08:29,258 --> 00:08:31,177
Gifted?

129
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:32,261
Mm.

130
00:08:34,388 --> 00:08:35,765
Really?

131
00:08:35,848 --> 00:08:39,685
And if it interests you two,
he said he would love to introduce her

132
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:41,771
to a top art school professor.

133
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:43,064
How does that sound?

134
00:08:43,731 --> 00:08:45,566
That sounds amazing.

135
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,443
That's great.

136
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,028
Just the other day,

137
00:08:49,111 --> 00:08:51,656
she said she wanted to be a doctor,
which is ridiculous.

138
00:08:51,739 --> 00:08:54,492
I said, "Absolutely not,"
and to go into something less expensive.

139
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:58,913
Really? That's an incredible goal as well.

140
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:01,332
Fumi.

141
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:04,877
Why don't we get him to introduce you
to an art professor? Okay?

142
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:14,011
Changing the monitor now.

143
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:21,227
Ms. Numata? Can you hear me?

144
00:09:21,727 --> 00:09:22,728
Get the doctor.

145
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:23,854
Right away.

146
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,316
Numata!

147
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:28,985
Can you hear me?

148
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:31,445
Numata?

149
00:09:42,290 --> 00:09:43,916
Oh, thank goodness.

150
00:09:44,417 --> 00:09:47,169
Take over for Dr. Numata? What?

151
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:49,755
It's an emergency.
Could you do it, please?

152
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:50,840
No. Not possible.

153
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:52,091
Please. You have to do it.

154
00:09:52,174 --> 00:09:53,968
- Not a chance.
- Come on, Dr. Hikita.

155
00:09:54,051 --> 00:09:55,928
It's a breach of contract.

156
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:57,638
The agreement is, I don't show my face.

157
00:09:57,722 --> 00:10:00,808
It would only be temporary. Just until
we can find another doctor to replace you.

158
00:10:00,891 --> 00:10:02,435
I can't.

159
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:06,272
I don't… I don't wanna talk
to patients anymore.

160
00:10:06,355 --> 00:10:09,692
I don't wanna give someone the opportunity
to file another harassment complaint.

161
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:10,651
Huh.

162
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:11,777
Huh?

163
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:16,115
And what if you use this?

164
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:17,074
Huh?

165
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:22,872
This way, you could stay anonymous.

166
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:25,916
No, no.

167
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:31,672
Find any promising candidates?

168
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:34,050
Yes, I found a few
from that headhunter's list

169
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:35,551
that was put together.

170
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:49,023
Something wrong?

171
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:53,527
Uh, Dr. Numata's file.

172
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:58,157
And this was put together by

173
00:10:58,908 --> 00:10:59,742
Takashina?

174
00:10:59,825 --> 00:11:01,285
Yeah, I think so.

175
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:02,787
Could you call him in, please?

176
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:04,288
Yes, no problem.

177
00:11:04,955 --> 00:11:06,332
Excuse me, could you call in…

178
00:11:06,415 --> 00:11:09,585
Hello, ma'am.
How are you today? Doing well?

179
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:12,421
Yes, thank you very much.

180
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,340
Take care of yourself, okay?

181
00:11:14,423 --> 00:11:17,968
The change of seasons
can be quite tough on the body, all right?

182
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:20,429
Thank you very much.

183
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:21,889
Sorry to disturb you.

184
00:11:22,848 --> 00:11:24,558
Mr. Konoike is here.

185
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:26,060
He'd like to have a word.

186
00:11:26,644 --> 00:11:27,645
Oh. Here?

187
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:29,730
I was told
he's in the building right now, sir.

188
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:34,068
Hello, Governor.

189
00:11:34,151 --> 00:11:37,071
Mr. Konoike, it's been a while, hasn't it?

190
00:11:37,154 --> 00:11:38,698
To what do I owe the pleasure?

191
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,116
Well, it just so happens

192
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:42,910
that I was already meeting someone
around here.

193
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:46,789
In fact, I know

194
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:49,333
someone who would
appreciate meeting you, Governor.

195
00:11:53,003 --> 00:11:54,171
Chairman.

196
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:55,673
Governor.

197
00:11:56,173 --> 00:11:58,050
Congratulations on your reelection.

198
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:02,513
So, the chairman just put this together?

199
00:12:02,596 --> 00:12:05,558
Correct, and things
such as the technical evaluation

200
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:07,226
were based on his opinion.

201
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:10,896
Understood. Thank you.

202
00:12:19,739 --> 00:12:21,031
Is there something else?

203
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:21,991
Uh…

204
00:12:22,867 --> 00:12:24,326
My apologies.

205
00:12:25,244 --> 00:12:28,330
I have something I'd like to discuss.

206
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,795
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

207
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:44,180
Are you going to the chairman?

208
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:55,608
So it was you who leaked the information.

209
00:12:57,276 --> 00:13:01,071
Well, seeing as you were
the chairman's lap dog,

210
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,448
this is unsurprising.

211
00:13:02,531 --> 00:13:03,824
- Uh…
- No, it's fine.

212
00:13:04,408 --> 00:13:06,327
Please, there's no need
to say anything at all.

213
00:13:12,249 --> 00:13:13,751
Get out of my sight right now.

214
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:50,830
Ando, I'm guessing Dad asked you
to spy on me as well?

215
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:53,499
Excuse me? What do you mean "spy on"?

216
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:55,668
I was just worried, is all.

217
00:13:55,751 --> 00:13:58,254
There's no need for you to worry about me.

218
00:13:58,337 --> 00:13:59,463
<i>That right?</i>

219
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:03,384
I heard Dr. Numata, the new hire
you met at the press conference,

220
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:05,928
is already on leave.

221
00:14:07,304 --> 00:14:11,058
Relax, okay? Stop being suspicious,
and just hear me out.

222
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:14,645
<i>I'm actually more pissed off at Dr. Arata.</i>

223
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:17,147
<i>He keeps poaching my doctors, too,</i>

224
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:21,861
and it's always with the same sales pitch
about how chain clinics are the worst.

225
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:23,821
<i>Hey, Rin?</i>

226
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:27,366
What do you say
we work together against him?

227
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:47,136
Are you ready, Fumi?

228
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:49,555
Do it.

229
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:59,106
Try not to be too surprised.

230
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:10,367
As a cosmetic surgeon,
what do you think of this?

231
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:11,702
Oh God.

232
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:13,746
Florida?

233
00:15:13,829 --> 00:15:15,789
<i>Plan is to open a clinic there next year.</i>

234
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:18,542
And expand into South Korea and Singapore.

235
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:21,378
My idea was to go there myself
and be the director,

236
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:24,048
but I was thinking maybe
I could leave it to you.

237
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:26,425
<i>Running the business here,</i>

238
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:29,595
<i>bending to the old guard in this country,</i>
<i>is exhausting, isn't it?</i>

239
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,096
Look, Rin.

240
00:15:31,722 --> 00:15:34,183
Leave him the Tohyama brand.
It's for the best.

241
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,519
<i>- I'm not kidding. You should…</i>
- No, sorry but…

242
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,440
I still have a…

243
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:44,485
a few things I need to do here.

244
00:15:46,528 --> 00:15:47,696
I'm very sorry.

245
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:57,456
You should rest up
while the swelling goes down. Okay?

246
00:16:00,584 --> 00:16:02,586
- Hey.
- Huh?

247
00:16:03,671 --> 00:16:06,465
I'm… bored.

248
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:08,300
You're bored?

249
00:16:09,176 --> 00:16:10,010
I can imagine.

250
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:12,596
Fortunately, that's not lethal, right?

251
00:16:13,263 --> 00:16:14,640
Just take it easy.

252
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:17,893
In cosmetic surgery,
you call it "recovery time."

253
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:23,899
When you're healed up,

254
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:27,194
we'll talk to the plastic surgeon
about facial reconstruction options.

255
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:31,365
Yes.

256
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:36,203
Okay. Why don't we discuss terms, then?

257
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:37,621
Great.

258
00:16:38,747 --> 00:16:40,624
Thank you. We'll talk again soon.

259
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:46,005
Oh, thanks.

260
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:49,341
Take a load off, huh?

261
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:52,511
I'm good.

262
00:16:53,637 --> 00:16:56,473
I'm here, having a normal meal, aren't I?

263
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:58,475
I meant at the clinic.

264
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:01,061
Why not close it for a while?

265
00:17:02,604 --> 00:17:04,481
Uh, I'm not sure I'm following?

266
00:17:04,565 --> 00:17:07,443
You should wait for Dr. Numata to recover.

267
00:17:08,444 --> 00:17:10,988
I told you, Dr. Numata wants to quit.

268
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:14,616
Yes, but you haven't accepted
her resignation yet, have you?

269
00:17:17,077 --> 00:17:18,829
I know you can't find another doctor

270
00:17:18,912 --> 00:17:20,664
that you could trust
as much as you trust her.

271
00:17:22,332 --> 00:17:25,461
So, why don't you wait
until she's recovered, then?

272
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,048
But if…

273
00:17:31,008 --> 00:17:32,051
I close the clinic now,

274
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,844
who do you think
that will end up benefiting?

275
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:35,804
So what if it does?

276
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:40,726
Sure, her connection to the chairman
was surprising.

277
00:17:40,809 --> 00:17:45,064
But Dr. Numata went her whole life
not knowing who her father was,

278
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:46,815
and there's nothing you can do about it.

279
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:49,902
If you accept that, I know she'll stay.

280
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:50,819
No.

281
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:57,618
I just can't do that.

282
00:17:57,701 --> 00:17:58,744
Oh, yeah?

283
00:17:59,578 --> 00:18:00,746
And why is that?

284
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:05,918
You don't understand.

285
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:07,628
No, I'm afraid I don't get it.

286
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:11,590
Jeez. Are family connections and blood
really that important?

287
00:18:12,299 --> 00:18:14,760
So what?
She's the chairman's daughter. Whatever.

288
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:19,973
It makes no difference to the patients
who come to the Tohyama Clinic for help.

289
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,434
Lily! You don't get it at all!

290
00:18:30,818 --> 00:18:32,986
This isn't like you, Rin. Just talk to me.

291
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:36,406
I had no clue
you could be this insensitive.

292
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,283
Would you like to tell me
where you're going?

293
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:56,677
Don't be too long, okay?

294
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:29,668
My apologies

295
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:32,129
for visiting so late.

296
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:38,677
I want to talk about
your resignation letter.

297
00:19:41,763 --> 00:19:43,807
I felt things were left in the air,

298
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,059
which isn't good

299
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:48,604
for you

300
00:19:49,813 --> 00:19:50,981
or for me.

301
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:54,818
That's why tomorrow,

302
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:58,780
I'll begin the paperwork
for your resignation.

303
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:04,536
And as for the 200 million,

304
00:20:05,913 --> 00:20:07,581
you don't need to pay me back.

305
00:20:11,084 --> 00:20:12,920
I have caused you

306
00:20:15,881 --> 00:20:18,467
more than enough pain already.

307
00:20:23,472 --> 00:20:24,806
Going forward…

308
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:29,436
we'll go our separate ways…

309
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:34,775
and hope for the best.

310
00:21:07,891 --> 00:21:09,685
MS. FUMI NUMATA

311
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:17,609
Back again?

312
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:21,530
I guess you should move in here.

313
00:21:26,034 --> 00:21:27,869
Hi.

314
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:29,204
Huh?

315
00:21:29,955 --> 00:21:32,708
O… Okura.

316
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:35,168
Look at you!

317
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:44,219
So, Dr. Tanuma, you used to be at
Musashino University Hospital, right?

318
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:46,596
Yeah, for around ten years.

319
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,307
The department chief was a real pain.

320
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:50,309
hat a relief that is.

321
00:21:50,809 --> 00:21:52,769
I thought you might be a new doctor.

322
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:54,313
Mm, well, to be honest,

323
00:21:54,396 --> 00:21:56,898
even doctors
with general medical experience

324
00:21:56,982 --> 00:21:59,443
can actually be just as bad or worse.

325
00:21:59,943 --> 00:22:02,029
Let's continue with the dissection.

326
00:22:02,112 --> 00:22:03,030
Yes.

327
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:11,705
Yes. Good job.

328
00:22:11,788 --> 00:22:12,831
<i>No way!</i>

329
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:15,876
You did a double-eyelid surgery on Takeru?

330
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:17,336
You got it.

331
00:22:17,419 --> 00:22:21,131
Then, you're telling me
your last cosmetic surgery

332
00:22:21,214 --> 00:22:22,174
was on your brother?

333
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:24,885
Yeah.

334
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:26,386
You're kidding?

335
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:28,305
I can't believe that! That's insane!

336
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:29,514
Insane?

337
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:34,519
So if that's the case,

338
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:37,272
would you be willing
to do my surgery next, then?

339
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,232
What?

340
00:22:39,316 --> 00:22:41,485
Wh… Why?

341
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:47,199
But… I already quit.

342
00:22:47,282 --> 00:22:48,658
No.

343
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:57,167
TOKYO GLOBAL BEAUTY HUB PROJECT

344
00:23:00,253 --> 00:23:02,589
FIRST CONFERENCE DETAILS

345
00:23:07,886 --> 00:23:10,138
Here we go!

346
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:15,560
This is seriously insane.

347
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:22,984
Hold on. Are you Takeru?

348
00:23:23,902 --> 00:23:27,072
I'm happy we get
to finally meet each other.

349
00:23:27,155 --> 00:23:29,449
Hey. Come in. I was just leaving.

350
00:23:31,284 --> 00:23:32,786
Okura.

351
00:23:36,832 --> 00:23:37,874
Thank you.

352
00:23:37,958 --> 00:23:40,919
Oh no, don't worry about it.
Not how I wanted it to end either.

353
00:23:43,422 --> 00:23:49,052
Well, just remember to enjoy
your well-deserved recovery time, okay?

354
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:51,346
Enjoy?

355
00:23:52,722 --> 00:23:54,099
Of course.

356
00:23:54,182 --> 00:23:57,102
It can't get any worse. You agree?

357
00:23:58,019 --> 00:23:59,354
Mm. Yeah, sure.

358
00:24:00,605 --> 00:24:01,982
While you recover,

359
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:05,610
try to believe that you're becoming
the best version of yourself.

360
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:09,698
If you try, even just for a moment,

361
00:24:09,781 --> 00:24:11,199
you'll feel invincible.

362
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:15,203
Okay.

363
00:24:20,667 --> 00:24:21,877
Be seeing ya.

364
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:24,921
Yeah.

365
00:24:27,632 --> 00:24:28,925
Bye-bye.

366
00:24:29,009 --> 00:24:31,011
Bye-bye.

367
00:24:41,021 --> 00:24:42,939
Want anything to drink?

368
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:49,362
Yeah.

369
00:24:59,831 --> 00:25:01,333
Macky.

370
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:03,960
Macky?

371
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:05,378
How is he?

372
00:25:06,087 --> 00:25:07,422
Oh, he's okay.

373
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:10,091
You probably shouldn't see him yet.

374
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:14,471
He seems to be struggling pretty hard.

375
00:25:20,852 --> 00:25:22,979
- Hey, Takeru.
- Hmm?

376
00:25:24,731 --> 00:25:26,650
I wanna see your eyes.

377
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:41,998
Not bad.

378
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:42,916
Thank you.

379
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:45,710
You'd rather hide them?

380
00:25:46,294 --> 00:25:47,128
For now.

381
00:25:48,171 --> 00:25:49,005
For now.

382
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,259
Hmm.

383
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:56,221
By the way,

384
00:25:57,806 --> 00:25:59,808
what'll you do after being discharged?

385
00:26:00,559 --> 00:26:04,479
Apparently, Dad needs a hostess
for the snack bar.

386
00:26:05,230 --> 00:26:06,606
Uh…

387
00:26:09,192 --> 00:26:12,320
Maybe I'll try art school.

388
00:26:12,904 --> 00:26:13,989
Art school?

389
00:26:14,072 --> 00:26:15,907
- Art school.
- Why?

390
00:26:15,991 --> 00:26:17,867
Well, I'm

391
00:26:18,994 --> 00:26:20,579
decent with my hands, right?

392
00:26:21,705 --> 00:26:22,622
Yeah, sure.

393
00:26:23,957 --> 00:26:25,750
When I was a kid…

394
00:26:28,169 --> 00:26:30,714
my teacher said
I should look into an art school.

395
00:26:31,548 --> 00:26:32,632
And so you applied?

396
00:26:34,092 --> 00:26:35,385
Nah, I just checked it out.

397
00:26:35,468 --> 00:26:37,137
Mm.

398
00:26:37,679 --> 00:26:39,514
Our mother…

399
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:40,432
Mm?

400
00:26:42,601 --> 00:26:44,394
…left before the visit ended.

401
00:26:47,147 --> 00:26:48,481
What? Why?

402
00:26:49,482 --> 00:26:54,070
I was just a grade school kid,
and she left me there.

403
00:26:55,488 --> 00:26:58,575
Kinda crazy, huh?

404
00:27:01,036 --> 00:27:02,996
I was devastated.

405
00:27:04,956 --> 00:27:06,374
I wanted to get even.

406
00:27:07,584 --> 00:27:10,837
Mom hated doctors, so I became one.

407
00:27:12,964 --> 00:27:14,633
So that's why you became a doctor.

408
00:27:15,508 --> 00:27:16,343
Exactly.

409
00:27:16,426 --> 00:27:18,595
Jeez, Fumi.

410
00:27:22,515 --> 00:27:24,017
Can you believe it?

411
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:27,437
That's how sad I was.

412
00:27:31,191 --> 00:27:32,233
Thanks, by the way.

413
00:27:33,485 --> 00:27:34,319
Huh?

414
00:27:39,532 --> 00:27:41,076
For doing my surgery.

415
00:27:46,373 --> 00:27:47,999
Of course.

416
00:28:26,329 --> 00:28:30,500
RECOVERY TIME IS IMPORTANT FOR
A CHRYSALIS TO BREAK OUT OF ITS COCOON

417
00:28:30,583 --> 00:28:32,794
AND TRANSFORM INTO A BUTTERFLY

418
00:28:32,877 --> 00:28:37,674
INSIDE THE CHRYSALIS, THE LARVAL TISSUES
ARE COMPLETELY DECONSTRUCTED

419
00:29:01,740 --> 00:29:03,241
Hurry up, Fumi!

420
00:29:03,783 --> 00:29:05,034
We're gonna be late!

421
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:16,129
Apparently, this teacher is amazing.

422
00:29:16,212 --> 00:29:19,340
I heard he even works on
designing churches in Spain.

423
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:29,142
What's wrong, Mom?

424
00:29:41,237 --> 00:29:42,489
Mommy?

425
00:29:45,283 --> 00:29:46,659
Mommy?

426
00:29:59,214 --> 00:30:00,381
Hi.

427
00:30:01,299 --> 00:30:02,967
- It's Tohyama.
- Ms. Tohyama.

428
00:30:03,051 --> 00:30:04,677
Yes, I see. Right.

429
00:30:04,761 --> 00:30:07,055
Excellent. I'll show you to your table.
Right over here.

430
00:30:07,931 --> 00:30:09,140
Excuse us.

431
00:30:09,224 --> 00:30:12,101
Well, for the cheek and jawbones,

432
00:30:12,185 --> 00:30:14,103
we'll use plates made of titanium

433
00:30:14,187 --> 00:30:17,023
and proceed with the nasal bone.

434
00:30:18,733 --> 00:30:20,318
After, we'll monitor your progress.

435
00:30:20,401 --> 00:30:22,195
Then, the next step, I believe,

436
00:30:22,278 --> 00:30:25,698
would be to use a prosthesis
for nasal reconstruction.

437
00:30:26,282 --> 00:30:27,116
F…

438
00:30:27,951 --> 00:30:28,993
Uh, yes?

439
00:30:31,454 --> 00:30:34,123
It's the same as cosmetic surgery.

440
00:30:35,166 --> 00:30:38,127
Pardon me,
but we're hardly on the same level.

441
00:30:44,509 --> 00:30:46,261
So what's next?

442
00:30:46,344 --> 00:30:51,724
Well, this afternoon, I have
an intramedullary nailing operation.

443
00:30:51,808 --> 00:30:53,434
Mm.

444
00:30:53,518 --> 00:30:55,311
So anyway, Numata,

445
00:30:56,354 --> 00:30:58,481
after being discharged,

446
00:30:59,190 --> 00:31:01,359
why don't you come back to work here?

447
00:31:03,403 --> 00:31:05,655
I spoke to the hospital director.
Don't worry.

448
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:09,450
As long as you're okay with it,
he's on board.

449
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:13,246
What do you know?

450
00:31:14,414 --> 00:31:16,040
Now they want me back?

451
00:31:16,124 --> 00:31:17,250
Uh, what?

452
00:31:18,126 --> 00:31:19,168
You're not happy with that?

453
00:31:20,169 --> 00:31:22,130
Mm.

454
00:31:22,964 --> 00:31:23,840
Okay.

455
00:31:24,549 --> 00:31:26,843
Take your time to think about it, Numata.

456
00:31:26,926 --> 00:31:28,428
Please try not to take forever though.

457
00:31:28,511 --> 00:31:30,263
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Hmm?

458
00:31:31,306 --> 00:31:32,432
Hey.

459
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:34,017
Him?

460
00:31:34,517 --> 00:31:35,602
Yo.

461
00:31:36,269 --> 00:31:37,770
Hey.

462
00:31:41,441 --> 00:31:42,859
This table right here.

463
00:31:46,029 --> 00:31:47,614
- You kidding? Here?
- What?

464
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:49,324
This is where I was told to bring you.

465
00:31:49,407 --> 00:31:51,659
- Why not by the stage?
- There he is.

466
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:19,228
Attention, please! Take your seats.
We're going to begin the conference.

467
00:32:19,854 --> 00:32:20,855
Director.

468
00:32:25,818 --> 00:32:28,112
- What the…
- Director.

469
00:32:30,031 --> 00:32:31,115
Whoa! Director…

470
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:37,789
Are you…

471
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:42,168
Are you gonna take
everything away from me?

472
00:32:47,882 --> 00:32:48,758
Well?

473
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:51,928
Go on!

474
00:32:53,346 --> 00:32:55,223
Tell me why you're going this far!

475
00:32:57,558 --> 00:32:58,977
I'm willing to do

476
00:33:00,436 --> 00:33:02,438
whatever it takes
to protect what's important to me.

477
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:06,609
And what's important?

478
00:33:09,570 --> 00:33:11,030
Is it Tohyama?

479
00:33:12,365 --> 00:33:14,492
Is it more important than family?

480
00:33:14,575 --> 00:33:16,661
Because you've completely lost it!

481
00:33:29,674 --> 00:33:31,509
We all have something.

482
00:33:32,135 --> 00:33:34,429
Something we don't wanna have taken
from us.

483
00:33:35,596 --> 00:33:37,640
Something important we don't wanna lose.

484
00:33:52,238 --> 00:33:53,072
My apologies.

485
00:33:53,614 --> 00:33:55,616
Sorry, everyone. Let's carry on.

486
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:58,036
All right, everybody. Please simmer down.

487
00:33:58,119 --> 00:33:59,787
Let's begin the conference!

488
00:34:00,621 --> 00:34:02,040
Take your seats, please.

489
00:34:02,123 --> 00:34:04,751
Please, everyone.
We ask for your cooperation.

490
00:34:04,834 --> 00:34:07,336
If we can all settle down,
we have a short amount of time.

491
00:34:07,420 --> 00:34:09,672
We kindly ask for your cooperation.

492
00:34:11,090 --> 00:34:12,258
Hey.

493
00:34:17,096 --> 00:34:18,473
You know…

494
00:34:21,809 --> 00:34:24,687
this was probably for the best.

495
00:34:28,858 --> 00:34:30,443
How could you even think that?

496
00:34:31,903 --> 00:34:32,987
Look.

497
00:34:33,821 --> 00:34:35,031
Honestly…

498
00:34:38,284 --> 00:34:41,746
it gave me a chance to think

499
00:34:43,164 --> 00:34:44,373
about my life.

500
00:34:46,626 --> 00:34:47,627
Oh, yeah?

501
00:34:48,878 --> 00:34:49,796
Hmm.

502
00:34:58,179 --> 00:34:59,013
Hey.

503
00:34:59,097 --> 00:35:00,556
Hold on a sec.

504
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:03,518
- Get closer.
- Uh, yeah, yeah. Just gimme a second.

505
00:35:04,894 --> 00:35:05,978
Mm.

506
00:35:09,732 --> 00:35:11,692
Ah, there you are.

507
00:35:14,362 --> 00:35:16,114
Hey, Macky.

508
00:35:17,073 --> 00:35:20,451
You can't work at the snack bar forever.

509
00:35:20,535 --> 00:35:22,203
You know that, right?

510
00:35:24,789 --> 00:35:25,790
Hmm.

511
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:35,216
Okay, but…

512
00:35:37,260 --> 00:35:38,469
Hmm?

513
00:35:40,429 --> 00:35:41,430
What if…

514
00:35:47,061 --> 00:35:49,522
What if I keep working
at the snack bar forever?

515
00:36:04,162 --> 00:36:05,580
Do whatever you want.

516
00:36:19,886 --> 00:36:21,012
Thank you.

517
00:36:58,966 --> 00:36:59,800
Stop! Stop!

518
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:01,052
Please, stop.

519
00:37:01,135 --> 00:37:02,553
Stop. Please, stop, stop.

520
00:37:02,637 --> 00:37:04,472
Stop it! Please, stop.

521
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:05,890
Stop it!

522
00:37:09,227 --> 00:37:10,228
Director?

523
00:37:12,647 --> 00:37:13,981
Pardon me, but…

524
00:37:15,483 --> 00:37:17,443
It's Ms. Konoike. She, um…

525
00:37:18,611 --> 00:37:20,279
She fell hard on her face.

526
00:37:20,363 --> 00:37:22,240
Call a damn ambulance, then!

527
00:37:22,323 --> 00:37:25,326
- She's already on her way here.
- This is a cosmetic surgery clinic!

528
00:37:27,161 --> 00:37:28,704
But she's already on her way.

529
00:37:40,091 --> 00:37:42,134
- Let go of me! No!
- Please sit down.

530
00:37:42,218 --> 00:37:44,595
- Calm down. Please sit. Right here.
- Let go! Let…

531
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:45,972
I need you to sit in the chair.

532
00:37:46,055 --> 00:37:47,765
- Ms. Konoike, please calm down.
- No!

533
00:37:47,848 --> 00:37:50,268
- Help me! I need help now! It hurts.
- Please. Sara.

534
00:37:50,351 --> 00:37:51,394
It hurts so much! It hurts!

535
00:37:51,477 --> 00:37:53,271
- See, Dr. Rin is here.
- Take it easy!

536
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:54,772
Calm down!

537
00:37:54,855 --> 00:37:56,148
I'm gonna call an ambulance.

538
00:37:56,232 --> 00:37:58,234
You need to go to the hospital
to be examined, okay?

539
00:37:58,317 --> 00:37:59,610
No, you can't do that to me!

540
00:37:59,694 --> 00:38:01,237
We can't do X-rays here.

541
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:03,114
You promised to take care of me forever!

542
00:38:03,197 --> 00:38:04,991
Sara! Listen!

543
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:15,376
I'm only doing this
for your own good, all right?

544
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:21,674
I'm gonna call your family, okay?

545
00:38:23,217 --> 00:38:24,510
But you promised.

546
00:38:24,593 --> 00:38:26,095
You promised.

547
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:30,433
You gave me your word you wouldn't.

548
00:38:32,768 --> 00:38:33,853
Please, Rin.

549
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:37,064
I don't care.

550
00:38:37,648 --> 00:38:39,859
I need you to treat me here.

551
00:38:41,694 --> 00:38:42,695
Rin.

552
00:38:49,910 --> 00:38:50,995
Director.

553
00:38:52,788 --> 00:38:54,498
I'll do it. Don't worry.

554
00:38:54,582 --> 00:38:56,125
I'll handle her surgery.

555
00:39:00,963 --> 00:39:01,797
I'll…

556
00:39:05,593 --> 00:39:06,594
I'll do it.

557
00:39:18,939 --> 00:39:22,234
<i>The first conference</i>
<i>for the Tokyo Global Beauty Hub Project</i>

558
00:39:22,318 --> 00:39:23,819
<i>was held today.</i>

559
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:25,613
<i>Ambassador Mr. Arata Tohyama,</i>

560
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:28,657
<i>former director</i>
<i>of the Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic,</i>

561
00:39:28,741 --> 00:39:30,659
<i>was among those in attendance.</i>

562
00:39:31,160 --> 00:39:32,453
<i>The atmosphere at the Tokyo…</i>

563
00:39:32,536 --> 00:39:33,621
Excuse me.

564
00:39:34,789 --> 00:39:37,833
I'll be taking you
to the operating room now.

565
00:39:39,794 --> 00:39:41,295
- Scalpel.
- Here.

566
00:40:04,318 --> 00:40:06,278
- Ms. Fumi Numata is ready.
- Okay.

567
00:40:06,362 --> 00:40:08,322
- Shall we begin?
- Yes.

568
00:40:19,834 --> 00:40:22,211
She should go to the ER.

569
00:40:22,795 --> 00:40:25,256
- It'll be fine.
- But we can't treat her here.

570
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:49,864
Director.

571
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:52,491
We can't do this.

572
00:40:56,495 --> 00:40:59,373
The work of the successor
of the Hand of God.

573
00:41:23,314 --> 00:41:24,607
It's okay.

574
00:41:47,630 --> 00:41:48,589
I can do this.

575
00:41:59,225 --> 00:42:00,601
<i>All right, let's move her.</i>

576
00:42:07,149 --> 00:42:09,068
<i>Ms. Konoike mentioned a promise.</i>

577
00:42:10,569 --> 00:42:12,571
What did she mean by that?

578
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:21,247
Truth is that she…

579
00:42:23,999 --> 00:42:26,502
She's never told her family

580
00:42:26,585 --> 00:42:28,087
that she lost…

581
00:42:30,172 --> 00:42:32,174
sight cause of my mistake.

582
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:34,051
Huh?

583
00:42:36,095 --> 00:42:38,931
<i>And it looks like she never told them</i>

584
00:42:40,558 --> 00:42:43,227
<i>about having plastic surgery either.</i>

585
00:42:44,603 --> 00:42:46,772
Oh God. I…

586
00:42:47,523 --> 00:42:49,483
I'm such a damn idiot.

587
00:42:51,235 --> 00:42:56,407
When she… told me
she wanted to keep it from her…

588
00:42:57,741 --> 00:42:59,118
from her family…

589
00:43:01,453 --> 00:43:02,663
I figured

590
00:43:04,164 --> 00:43:07,376
I'd use the promise to hide my mistake.

591
00:43:09,295 --> 00:43:11,255
At least that's what I thought.

592
00:43:14,425 --> 00:43:17,720
I really only care about
looking out for myself.

593
00:43:23,392 --> 00:43:26,186
And that's why
I destroyed the clinic like I did.

594
00:43:41,493 --> 00:43:43,412
I'm going to close

595
00:43:45,247 --> 00:43:46,582
Tohyama Clinic.

596
00:44:16,945 --> 00:44:17,821
Take it easy.

597
00:44:19,073 --> 00:44:20,866
You're still under anesthesia.

598
00:44:21,659 --> 00:44:23,327
You've gone through a lot.

599
00:44:30,876 --> 00:44:32,211
Dr. Numata…

600
00:44:35,214 --> 00:44:36,799
it's very clear…

601
00:44:40,302 --> 00:44:41,845
that you're my daughter.

602
00:44:45,641 --> 00:44:46,767
Of course,

603
00:44:48,477 --> 00:44:50,688
I don't expect you to understand it all.

604
00:44:52,106 --> 00:44:52,940
But…

605
00:44:55,526 --> 00:44:57,903
I'm not sure how much time I have left.

606
00:44:59,321 --> 00:45:02,991
That surgery I had a while back
didn't exactly work.

607
00:45:04,243 --> 00:45:06,620
So I need to be precious about my time.

608
00:45:20,342 --> 00:45:21,802
Le…

609
00:45:21,885 --> 00:45:24,388
Let go. Let go.

610
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:29,351
Only now I realize

611
00:45:30,853 --> 00:45:32,396
what's actually important.

612
00:45:37,192 --> 00:45:38,360
It's blood.

613
00:45:46,869 --> 00:45:48,746
How could…

614
00:45:50,038 --> 00:45:51,331
How could I

615
00:45:52,541 --> 00:45:53,792
have been so foolish?

616
00:45:56,378 --> 00:45:59,131
Someone of my own blood…

617
00:46:02,968 --> 00:46:04,720
was there all along, and yet…

618
00:46:09,683 --> 00:46:11,101
Could you be the one…

619
00:46:14,188 --> 00:46:15,856
to carry on our bloodline?

620
00:46:20,611 --> 00:46:21,945
Cheers.

621
00:46:30,829 --> 00:46:32,748
I still remember

622
00:46:33,332 --> 00:46:36,001
the first time I assisted you in surgery.

623
00:46:36,668 --> 00:46:37,878
I can say this now.

624
00:46:39,213 --> 00:46:40,672
I saw your genius.

625
00:46:42,049 --> 00:46:45,302
I had never seen a facelift performed
that quickly.

626
00:46:46,386 --> 00:46:48,514
The result was perfection.

627
00:46:52,100 --> 00:46:54,269
In that moment, I knew that

628
00:46:55,604 --> 00:46:59,650
"The Hand of God" exists,
and I get to work with someone incredible.

629
00:47:05,906 --> 00:47:07,699
I take back closing the clinic.

630
00:47:08,450 --> 00:47:10,327
Huh?

631
00:47:12,579 --> 00:47:14,498
Just joking.

632
00:47:17,501 --> 00:47:19,545
I'm not a genius. You know that?

633
00:47:19,628 --> 00:47:22,089
The other doctors would throw a fit
if they heard you say that.

634
00:47:22,172 --> 00:47:23,006
I'm dead serious.

635
00:47:24,967 --> 00:47:26,176
Ever since…

636
00:47:27,719 --> 00:47:31,849
Ever since I was a kid,
I screwed up everything.

637
00:47:33,433 --> 00:47:36,436
And 'cause of that,
I've always had insecurities.

638
00:47:39,690 --> 00:47:43,026
It must have been
when I started junior high.

639
00:47:45,112 --> 00:47:46,572
I went on a TV show.

640
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:50,784
It was my dad's regular show.

641
00:47:51,493 --> 00:47:53,078
"Trust in the Hand of God."

642
00:47:53,161 --> 00:47:56,290
So then, while filming,

643
00:47:56,957 --> 00:47:58,584
suddenly, my dad,

644
00:47:58,667 --> 00:48:02,379
he announced I was to be his successor.

645
00:48:04,882 --> 00:48:08,594
On public TV,
in front of a massive studio audience.

646
00:48:10,804 --> 00:48:13,140
In any case, my dad was just…

647
00:48:13,223 --> 00:48:15,642
Well, I think
he was just putting on a show.

648
00:48:16,435 --> 00:48:19,396
Though as a child, it was…

649
00:48:21,982 --> 00:48:23,901
it was an incredible feeling.

650
00:48:27,279 --> 00:48:28,155
I…

651
00:48:30,157 --> 00:48:32,284
worked hard to be what I am.

652
00:48:33,619 --> 00:48:34,703
Well, then,

653
00:48:36,204 --> 00:48:37,831
your hard work really paid off.

654
00:48:40,125 --> 00:48:41,293
That's not it.

655
00:48:43,462 --> 00:48:46,798
All I had was the patience
to put in the time and effort.

656
00:48:48,884 --> 00:48:52,054
I'm pretty sure
my dad saw through it a long time ago.

657
00:48:54,056 --> 00:48:56,516
He knew I wasn't really
the next "Hand of God."

658
00:48:57,601 --> 00:49:02,064
So that means
the second Hand of God will be Rin?

659
00:49:03,065 --> 00:49:04,524
Well, I might be biased,

660
00:49:04,608 --> 00:49:07,694
but she's hardworking,
and I'm sure she'll be a great doctor.

661
00:49:08,278 --> 00:49:10,781
A worthy successor to the Tohyama name.

662
00:49:11,365 --> 00:49:12,282
And Rin?

663
00:49:12,366 --> 00:49:14,701
Any thoughts on what your dad just said?

664
00:49:15,202 --> 00:49:16,078
I'll try my best.

665
00:49:16,828 --> 00:49:18,538
She accepts! How exciting.

666
00:49:18,622 --> 00:49:20,457
I look forward to what she does
in the future.

667
00:49:21,083 --> 00:49:23,752
This week's Beauty Revolution
is brought to you live

668
00:49:23,835 --> 00:49:26,755
straight from
the Tokyo University of Fine Arts campus,

669
00:49:26,838 --> 00:49:29,549
where the school's festival
is in full swing!

670
00:49:29,633 --> 00:49:31,927
Well then, Doctor. Would you, please?

671
00:49:32,844 --> 00:49:36,431
Trust in The Hand of God.

672
00:49:55,409 --> 00:49:57,035
Thank you. Thank you.

673
00:49:58,745 --> 00:50:00,247
Thank you very much, everyone!

674
00:50:00,998 --> 00:50:02,082
Thank you.

675
00:50:03,750 --> 00:50:06,169
And don't forget
to watch the broadcast later!

676
00:50:06,253 --> 00:50:08,213
- Mommy!
- Thank you very much!

677
00:50:08,296 --> 00:50:10,007
Mommy, where are you going?

678
00:50:16,346 --> 00:50:17,472
Mommy!

679
00:50:36,783 --> 00:50:37,951
I'm sorry.

680
00:50:42,039 --> 00:50:43,498
I'm sorry, Lily.

681
00:50:47,836 --> 00:50:49,838
I always end up hurting you.

682
00:50:53,717 --> 00:50:54,968
I'm so sorry.

683
00:51:03,810 --> 00:51:04,770
Please forgive me.

684
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:17,949
You seem to have quite a vested interest
in the Tohyama name.

685
00:51:18,033 --> 00:51:19,409
Do you mind telling us

686
00:51:19,493 --> 00:51:22,537
what brought you to the decision
to let it go?

687
00:51:23,205 --> 00:51:25,373
<i>Well, a father knows</i>

688
00:51:25,457 --> 00:51:27,834
<i>when they're no match for their daughters.</i>

689
00:51:28,460 --> 00:51:31,421
I figured any more conflict
wouldn't be beneficial for either of us,

690
00:51:31,505 --> 00:51:33,048
so I decided to withdraw.

691
00:51:33,632 --> 00:51:36,635
<i>Are you planning to go ahead</i>
<i>with the new clinic opening?</i>

692
00:51:36,718 --> 00:51:38,011
<i>Well, on that subject,</i>

693
00:51:38,095 --> 00:51:39,846
I'll have to reconsider
the clinic's location,

694
00:51:39,930 --> 00:51:41,181
so as not to cause

695
00:51:41,264 --> 00:51:43,266
<i>any more issues with the Tohyama Clinic.</i>

696
00:51:43,850 --> 00:51:46,186
<i>I will be renaming it, after all.</i>

697
00:51:46,269 --> 00:51:49,064
Have there been discussions
with your daughter on all this?

698
00:51:49,147 --> 00:51:50,148
Director.

699
00:51:51,483 --> 00:51:52,818
<i>Did I talk to her?</i>

700
00:51:58,365 --> 00:51:59,241
<i>I'll leave it at that.</i>

701
00:51:59,324 --> 00:52:00,909
- <i>Oh.</i>
- <i>Mm.</i>

702
00:52:01,660 --> 00:52:04,287
Wait, you're not… coming back?

703
00:52:04,871 --> 00:52:05,747
No.

704
00:52:06,790 --> 00:52:09,126
So you… won't come back

705
00:52:09,209 --> 00:52:11,086
even though the hospital director said
you could?

706
00:52:16,216 --> 00:52:17,050
No, thanks.

707
00:52:18,426 --> 00:52:20,554
- You're sure?
- Yes.

708
00:52:21,429 --> 00:52:23,348
Jeez, what a waste.

709
00:52:24,266 --> 00:52:26,351
Can you imagine
how much we're going to lose?

710
00:52:28,228 --> 00:52:31,481
And you're sure
you want to give up the name too?

711
00:52:36,778 --> 00:52:38,071
Dr. Komiya.

712
00:52:41,992 --> 00:52:45,120
So then, you and I will work together?

713
00:52:47,122 --> 00:52:51,418
There's just one… condition.

714
00:52:52,711 --> 00:52:53,545
What do you mean?

715
00:52:54,671 --> 00:52:56,464
Tohyama.

716
00:52:59,926 --> 00:53:01,344
Give it up.

717
00:53:03,722 --> 00:53:05,390
Let her have the name.

718
00:53:13,190 --> 00:53:15,567
That's… what I want.

719
00:53:17,861 --> 00:53:19,029
Chairman.

720
00:53:19,654 --> 00:53:22,449
What do you mean there's been a delay
with opening the clinic?

721
00:53:23,450 --> 00:53:26,578
I've decided
to make some changes at the clinic.

722
00:53:27,621 --> 00:53:30,498
A new location with a new director.

723
00:53:32,334 --> 00:53:34,753
Don't worry.
I'll update you when necessary.

724
00:53:34,836 --> 00:53:35,921
But, Chairman Arata,

725
00:53:36,963 --> 00:53:39,090
I came here
just so I can work by your side.

726
00:53:40,800 --> 00:53:42,093
I deserve an explanation.

727
00:53:43,720 --> 00:53:45,889
Who'd you choose as the new director?

728
00:53:48,016 --> 00:53:51,478
Unfortunately, if working for me
is what you came for,

729
00:53:52,938 --> 00:53:54,481
I'll have to ask you to leave.

730
00:53:55,315 --> 00:53:56,149
What?

731
00:54:03,198 --> 00:54:06,284
Those who want an easy ride
on someone else's coattails,

732
00:54:07,744 --> 00:54:08,912
I have no use for.

733
00:54:14,793 --> 00:54:15,710
<i>All right.</i>

734
00:54:16,211 --> 00:54:17,879
I know whatever I say doesn't matter.

735
00:54:17,963 --> 00:54:20,423
It won't change your mind, anyways.

736
00:54:22,300 --> 00:54:24,970
Let me know
when you've decided what's next.

737
00:54:27,889 --> 00:54:28,848
Hold on.

738
00:54:29,808 --> 00:54:31,601
Hmm? What's up?

739
00:54:37,899 --> 00:54:39,401
Just one more thing.

740
00:54:40,068 --> 00:54:41,736
Just one more thing?

741
00:54:48,660 --> 00:54:49,661
It…

742
00:54:52,789 --> 00:54:55,583
has to do with my face.

743
00:54:56,084 --> 00:54:57,377
You're quitting?

744
00:54:57,460 --> 00:54:58,753
Yeah, today…

745
00:55:01,423 --> 00:55:03,133
will be my final day ever.

746
00:55:04,050 --> 00:55:07,053
But didn't the chairman
give up the Tohyama name?

747
00:55:09,806 --> 00:55:12,976
No, I won't let this happen.

748
00:55:13,059 --> 00:55:14,561
Or did you forget what you did, Rin?

749
00:55:14,644 --> 00:55:16,062
I haven't forgotten.

750
00:55:18,189 --> 00:55:19,482
I could never forget that.

751
00:55:21,484 --> 00:55:22,861
I'll forever…

752
00:55:24,863 --> 00:55:29,075
carry that mistake with me
for the rest of my life.

753
00:55:30,869 --> 00:55:31,911
But today…

754
00:55:31,995 --> 00:55:33,079
Well,

755
00:55:34,122 --> 00:55:37,083
I think that it's the best time
for us to end this arrangement.

756
00:55:40,420 --> 00:55:41,713
It's for the best.

757
00:55:41,796 --> 00:55:45,133
If we don't do this now,
we'll be stuck in this loop forever.

758
00:55:48,428 --> 00:55:50,388
It'll be painful at first, I know,

759
00:55:51,264 --> 00:55:53,266
but I need to make this all public.

760
00:55:55,435 --> 00:55:56,936
Does this mean you're gonna abandon me?

761
00:55:57,020 --> 00:55:58,146
Not at all.

762
00:55:58,646 --> 00:56:00,774
I promise I will never abandon you again.

763
00:56:02,108 --> 00:56:03,234
Even though

764
00:56:05,070 --> 00:56:06,780
today is my last day in practice,

765
00:56:07,989 --> 00:56:09,366
I'll be right there,

766
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:11,284
and I'm gonna make sure

767
00:56:11,368 --> 00:56:14,329
that you continue to receive
your treatments just as before.

768
00:56:15,330 --> 00:56:18,416
After all, we've known
each other for a long time.

769
00:56:23,296 --> 00:56:24,255
So…

770
00:56:26,257 --> 00:56:27,967
let's do this together, okay?

771
00:56:38,770 --> 00:56:39,854
It's gonna be okay.

772
00:56:45,693 --> 00:56:46,986
Really, Rin?

773
00:56:48,405 --> 00:56:49,239
Yeah.

774
00:56:49,948 --> 00:56:51,408
It's gonna be all right.

775
00:57:03,795 --> 00:57:05,672
Well, you called it, Director.

776
00:57:06,339 --> 00:57:10,176
The chairman is, in fact,
quite the sneaky bastard, after all.

777
00:57:10,969 --> 00:57:12,053
What are you saying?

778
00:57:12,137 --> 00:57:13,304
Numata.

779
00:57:13,930 --> 00:57:16,808
The chairman made her the director
of his new clinic.

780
00:57:18,226 --> 00:57:21,646
Dropping the Tohyama name
and canceling the Tokyo clinic opening

781
00:57:21,729 --> 00:57:23,690
were all a part of Numata's demands.

782
00:57:24,232 --> 00:57:25,400
Can you believe that?

783
00:57:37,287 --> 00:57:38,121
Takeru?

784
00:57:57,849 --> 00:58:00,059
The other day, I told you, right?

785
00:58:03,563 --> 00:58:05,482
That it's best we go our separate ways.

786
00:58:14,657 --> 00:58:16,284
I'm here today…

787
00:58:21,372 --> 00:58:22,790
as a patient.

788
00:58:25,877 --> 00:58:27,045
Director.

789
00:58:29,297 --> 00:58:30,715
I'm asking…

790
00:58:33,176 --> 00:58:34,969
for you to fix my face.

791
00:58:43,645 --> 00:58:44,979
And why me, then?

792
00:58:47,023 --> 00:58:48,983
This isn't personal.

793
00:58:54,072 --> 00:58:55,281
I just…

794
00:59:02,539 --> 00:59:05,208
need you to be the one to fix it.

795
00:59:10,255 --> 00:59:13,049
I looked down on cosmetic surgery.

796
00:59:15,468 --> 00:59:18,972
So this must be a bit of a shock to you.

797
00:59:20,974 --> 00:59:21,975
But then…

798
00:59:27,230 --> 00:59:28,982
working here, I've…

799
00:59:31,734 --> 00:59:34,112
I've met so many patients…

800
00:59:36,864 --> 00:59:38,324
which got me thinking,

801
00:59:39,117 --> 00:59:40,451
"Maybe…

802
00:59:44,163 --> 00:59:47,625
it's my turn to try to change myself."

803
00:59:50,503 --> 00:59:52,880
I always depended on others.

804
00:59:54,674 --> 00:59:57,885
Yet, my own family had no value to me.

805
00:59:59,887 --> 01:00:02,181
I want you to do my surgery.

806
01:00:09,188 --> 01:00:10,940
I want to change.

807
01:00:35,298 --> 01:00:36,215
Director.

808
01:00:39,761 --> 01:00:40,928
Please.

809
01:00:48,728 --> 01:00:49,896
Director.

810
01:00:59,530 --> 01:01:01,449
I'm asking for another chance.

811
01:01:07,664 --> 01:01:09,499
For new wings to fly.

812
01:01:33,481 --> 01:01:34,941
I also need…

813
01:01:37,360 --> 01:01:38,903
new wings so I can fly.

814
01:01:42,281 --> 01:01:44,701
Fumi, I need that as well.

815
01:01:47,787 --> 01:01:50,331
That's why I accepted your resignation…

816
01:01:53,710 --> 01:01:56,337
and made the decision to close the clinic.

817
01:01:59,340 --> 01:02:01,676
I want more than anything

818
01:02:02,635 --> 01:02:04,846
to move to the next stage as well.

819
01:02:21,696 --> 01:02:23,406
I cannot perform…

820
01:02:25,533 --> 01:02:26,701
your surgery.

821
01:02:30,830 --> 01:02:32,623
I'm very sorry.

822
01:02:38,004 --> 01:02:39,297
I understand.

823
01:02:42,425 --> 01:02:43,342
Of course.

824
01:02:48,431 --> 01:02:49,474
Thank you…

825
01:02:51,559 --> 01:02:52,518
Director.

826
01:03:09,368 --> 01:03:10,369
<i>In other news,</i>

827
01:03:10,453 --> 01:03:14,874
<i>this week will mark the closing</i>
<i>of Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic.</i>

828
01:03:14,957 --> 01:03:18,836
<i>A clinic with a long history,</i>
<i>dating back to the early Heisei era.</i>

829
01:03:19,337 --> 01:03:23,174
Perhaps having Tokyo
select highly skilled clinics

830
01:03:23,257 --> 01:03:24,717
and awarding them stars?

831
01:03:25,301 --> 01:03:27,261
Similar to Michelin stars?

832
01:03:27,345 --> 01:03:28,471
Yes, exactly.

833
01:03:28,554 --> 01:03:29,806
Huh. Great idea.

834
01:03:29,889 --> 01:03:32,642
That would make things much clearer
to the overseas clients.

835
01:03:32,725 --> 01:03:34,727
Very clever.

836
01:03:34,811 --> 01:03:37,396
<i>The sudden closure</i>
<i>has brought on criticism</i>

837
01:03:37,480 --> 01:03:39,524
<i>and shock from patients.</i>

838
01:03:39,607 --> 01:03:41,275
<i>As a way to ease the transition,</i>

839
01:03:41,359 --> 01:03:45,947
<i>Tohyama Cosmetic Surgery Clinic</i>
<i>has announced it will handle all transfers</i>

840
01:03:46,030 --> 01:03:51,577
<i>for patients that had made reservations</i>
<i>to the MDC Minatoku Beauty Clinic.</i>

841
01:04:16,060 --> 01:04:19,605
<i>Oh, hi Sara.</i>
<i>Wasn't expecting you. Come on in.</i>

842
01:04:21,440 --> 01:04:23,276
I'd like to talk to Grandfather.

843
01:04:33,119 --> 01:04:34,078
Oh.

844
01:04:37,206 --> 01:04:38,541
Takeru.

845
01:04:39,041 --> 01:04:39,917
Hmm?

846
01:04:40,918 --> 01:04:44,213
I'm saying goodbye to my old face.

847
01:04:46,173 --> 01:04:48,384
- Does that make you sad?
- Huh?

848
01:04:54,974 --> 01:04:57,727
Let's take a photo
to immortalize this moment

849
01:04:57,810 --> 01:04:59,312
before the surgery.

850
01:04:59,395 --> 01:05:01,439
Immortalize what?

851
01:05:01,522 --> 01:05:03,065
This?

852
01:05:03,149 --> 01:05:05,026
- Huh?
- Why not?

853
01:05:05,109 --> 01:05:06,444
I'll get Dad and the others.

854
01:05:06,527 --> 01:05:08,738
That's not necessary.

855
01:05:09,655 --> 01:05:12,408
What's there to immortalize?

856
01:05:31,385 --> 01:05:34,013
<i>Apparently, you delayed your flight back.</i>

857
01:05:34,096 --> 01:05:37,975
I just figured I would
take it easy over there for a while.

858
01:05:38,059 --> 01:05:39,226
So then,

859
01:05:40,353 --> 01:05:41,812
if you have no further issues,

860
01:05:41,896 --> 01:05:43,606
I'm going to be announcing the opening

861
01:05:43,689 --> 01:05:47,151
of the new Florida clinic
as early as next week.

862
01:05:47,652 --> 01:05:48,986
I'm okay, thanks.

863
01:05:49,070 --> 01:05:51,364
If you have ideas, you let me know.

864
01:05:51,447 --> 01:05:54,867
The Florida clinic will be yours to run
how you like, Rin.

865
01:05:56,911 --> 01:05:58,788
I fully trust your intuition.

866
01:06:00,456 --> 01:06:03,542
Let's see, red and black bookkeeping.

867
01:06:03,626 --> 01:06:05,127
<i>Thank you for waiting.</i>

868
01:06:06,170 --> 01:06:08,506
<i>…flight 62, bound for Los Angeles,</i>

869
01:06:08,589 --> 01:06:10,967
<i>departing at 11:05, is now ready…</i>

870
01:06:11,050 --> 01:06:13,010
NANAMI TODOROKI
HAVE A GREAT TRIP!

871
01:06:13,094 --> 01:06:15,888
<i>…first-class passengers,</i>
<i>top-tier status members…</i>

872
01:06:29,652 --> 01:06:30,695
The time's come.

873
01:06:30,778 --> 01:06:32,029
Mm.

874
01:06:35,491 --> 01:06:37,994
My face is in your hands now.

875
01:06:44,917 --> 01:06:46,585
- Have a safe trip, sir.
- Thank you.

876
01:06:47,420 --> 01:06:50,673
<i>Attention, please,</i>
<i>priority boarding is now in progress</i>

877
01:06:50,756 --> 01:06:51,882
<i>for JFL flight 62…</i>

878
01:06:51,966 --> 01:06:53,259
What's up?

879
01:06:53,342 --> 01:06:55,553
<i>…departing at 11:05,</i>

880
01:06:56,387 --> 01:06:57,221
Rin!

881
01:06:59,140 --> 01:07:03,686
TAKERU SENT ME THIS.
SOUNDS LIKE THE OPERATION IS STARTING NOW.

882
01:07:21,370 --> 01:07:22,538
I… I can't.

883
01:07:24,540 --> 01:07:25,666
I have to go back right away.

884
01:07:25,750 --> 01:07:27,585
What's going on? You feeling all right?

885
01:07:27,668 --> 01:07:29,920
I keep running away, even though…

886
01:07:31,881 --> 01:07:33,924
I knew all along what…

887
01:07:36,260 --> 01:07:37,428
actually matters.

888
01:08:13,798 --> 01:08:16,300
All right, I'll be placing a mask on you.

889
01:08:17,927 --> 01:08:19,804
Slow breaths, okay?

890
01:08:22,431 --> 01:08:23,933
Beginning anesthesia.

891
01:08:25,684 --> 01:08:27,728
You're gonna start feeling sleepy.

892
01:08:27,812 --> 01:08:29,021
You can't go in!

893
01:08:29,105 --> 01:08:31,273
- Huh? Hey!
- Stop! You can't go in!

894
01:08:31,816 --> 01:08:33,859
Dr. Tohyama?

895
01:08:38,489 --> 01:08:39,865
She asked me…

896
01:08:41,909 --> 01:08:43,452
She asked me to perform her surgery.

897
01:08:46,705 --> 01:08:48,624
She wanted me to be the one
to fix her face.

898
01:08:49,250 --> 01:08:51,210
I'm sorry, but it's too late for that.

899
01:08:51,293 --> 01:08:52,503
I'm begging you!

900
01:08:57,049 --> 01:08:58,008
It's the truth.

901
01:09:01,387 --> 01:09:04,223
I'm telling you, she asked me to do it.

902
01:09:10,938 --> 01:09:13,023
I'm the only one who can do it.

903
01:09:17,862 --> 01:09:19,530
To give her new wings.

904
01:09:36,172 --> 01:09:39,550
Hey, Dr. Rui here!
How is everybody out there doing?

905
01:09:39,633 --> 01:09:41,343
Someone special will be joining us

906
01:09:41,427 --> 01:09:44,096
on today's Cosmetic Surgery
for Beginners lesson.

907
01:09:44,180 --> 01:09:47,516
None other than
MBC's very own idol, Moenon!

908
01:09:47,600 --> 01:09:49,643
Hey!

909
01:09:49,727 --> 01:09:51,729
- It's me, Moenon.
- Adorable.

910
01:09:53,564 --> 01:09:57,151
We actually knew each other before MBC.
Isn't that right?

911
01:09:57,234 --> 01:09:58,485
Yeah, we did.

912
01:09:58,569 --> 01:10:01,822
And that was years
before you had plastic surgery, which was…

913
01:10:01,906 --> 01:10:05,117
I was in the fifth grade.
So around two years ago.

914
01:10:05,201 --> 01:10:06,327
- Mm.
- Yeah, that's right.

915
01:10:06,911 --> 01:10:08,078
- Two years ago.
- Oh wow.

916
01:10:08,162 --> 01:10:09,955
- Two years goes fast.
- It does.

917
01:10:10,039 --> 01:10:12,374
So that means
you're in junior high, right?

918
01:10:12,458 --> 01:10:14,793
Yeah, it's my first year of junior high.

919
01:10:14,877 --> 01:10:16,795
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

920
01:10:16,879 --> 01:10:18,214
Wait, so you decided?

921
01:10:18,297 --> 01:10:20,299
Hmm, I have.

922
01:10:20,799 --> 01:10:22,843
I talked with my mom yesterday.

923
01:10:23,802 --> 01:10:24,803
What'd she say?

924
01:10:25,304 --> 01:10:27,681
She said it was okay
to go for a consultation.

925
01:10:27,765 --> 01:10:31,101
I have to talk to her first
before deciding what to do next.

926
01:10:31,852 --> 01:10:34,146
Ah, so she might just say no, then.

927
01:10:35,105 --> 01:10:39,068
Hmm, basketball's kinda cool, but…

928
01:10:39,652 --> 01:10:41,362
Yeah, but I think I'll go with orchestra.

929
01:10:41,445 --> 01:10:44,031
- You sure?
- Yeah. So what'll you do?

930
01:10:44,114 --> 01:10:46,659
- I prefer music, so…
- Hmm.

931
01:10:46,742 --> 01:10:48,869
- I probably won't pick sports.
- What?

932
01:10:48,953 --> 01:10:51,413
- Definitely do sports.
- You're right!

933
01:10:54,625 --> 01:10:56,335
- I'm home.
- Hey, Takeru.

934
01:10:57,962 --> 01:10:59,046
Oh, hi, Mikana.

935
01:10:59,797 --> 01:11:00,631
Come in.

936
01:11:00,714 --> 01:11:03,676
She's actually here for a consultation.

937
01:11:03,759 --> 01:11:04,718
Seriously?

938
01:11:04,802 --> 01:11:06,804
You need your parents' consent though.

939
01:11:06,887 --> 01:11:08,681
It's okay
if it's just a consultation, right?

940
01:11:08,764 --> 01:11:09,848
Yeah, I guess.

941
01:11:09,932 --> 01:11:11,558
Well, here you go.

942
01:11:12,351 --> 01:11:13,394
Fill out this form.

943
01:11:13,477 --> 01:11:15,062
Thanks for coming in today.

944
01:11:15,688 --> 01:11:16,689
Thank you.

945
01:11:17,481 --> 01:11:20,651
- See you again next week, all right?
- Right. Next week.

946
01:11:20,734 --> 01:11:22,194
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

947
01:11:22,278 --> 01:11:23,988
- Take care.
- Thank you, bye!

948
01:11:26,949 --> 01:11:28,242
- Hey, Takeru.
- Hey, Maki.

949
01:11:28,325 --> 01:11:29,785
And your email goes here.

950
01:11:29,868 --> 01:11:31,578
Yeah, yeah. Just like that.

951
01:11:32,079 --> 01:11:33,914
Perfect. Don't forget dot com.

952
01:11:35,207 --> 01:11:37,584
Oh, don't worry. We have an opening now…

953
01:11:38,085 --> 01:11:39,044
Oh.

954
01:11:42,381 --> 01:11:43,257
Oh.

955
01:11:45,759 --> 01:11:47,344
Come in, please.

956
01:11:48,554 --> 01:11:50,931
Sorry… to interrupt.

957
01:12:01,608 --> 01:12:02,693
It's been a while.

958
01:12:05,821 --> 01:12:06,989
It has been.

959
01:12:16,665 --> 01:12:17,708
Here you go.

960
01:12:19,710 --> 01:12:23,339
I figured
you'd be working for the chairman.

961
01:12:23,422 --> 01:12:25,549
You closed Tohyama Clinic, so why would I?

962
01:12:27,259 --> 01:12:29,636
I didn't owe Tohyama anything anymore.

963
01:12:32,931 --> 01:12:34,266
Still, though.

964
01:12:36,769 --> 01:12:39,188
Wasn't expecting you
to open a cosmetic surgery clinic.

965
01:12:40,356 --> 01:12:42,066
I gotta earn a living.

966
01:12:42,149 --> 01:12:44,026
Besides, it's become
a bit of a family business.

967
01:12:44,902 --> 01:12:45,986
I can tell.

968
01:12:46,862 --> 01:12:48,238
Saw you on Insta.

969
01:12:49,490 --> 01:12:51,158
You did a lot of traveling

970
01:12:51,241 --> 01:12:53,452
to all sorts of countries,
lots of good food.

971
01:12:54,661 --> 01:12:56,663
Thought to myself,
"She's having a great time."

972
01:13:01,001 --> 01:13:03,087
- You mind if I look?
- Mm.

973
01:13:20,020 --> 01:13:21,105
You're gorgeous.

974
01:13:23,649 --> 01:13:24,900
You look perfect for me.

975
01:13:25,984 --> 01:13:27,361
Says the Hand of God herself.

976
01:13:34,118 --> 01:13:37,996
Are you finished with… cosmetic clinics?

977
01:13:38,080 --> 01:13:39,873
I'm finished.

978
01:13:41,792 --> 01:13:44,545
It's too much pain to build a new clinic
from the ground up.

979
01:13:44,628 --> 01:13:47,464
Yeah, isn't that the truth, huh?

980
01:13:49,216 --> 01:13:50,217
Though…

981
01:13:52,219 --> 01:13:54,680
I could see myself buying a small clinic

982
01:13:55,931 --> 01:13:58,475
and taking over as the director.

983
01:13:58,559 --> 01:14:00,227
Oh.

984
01:14:00,978 --> 01:14:02,646
I see.

985
01:14:03,272 --> 01:14:07,151
People who always solve everything
with money work on a different level.

986
01:14:10,654 --> 01:14:11,488
Hmm?

987
01:14:20,372 --> 01:14:21,957
Two hundred million work?
